  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0155_141198a520ee.png\" /> The conjugate acid is stabilized by resonance with two different <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group.<br/><br/> <img src=\"assets\\st0155_0bcd7666507c.png\" /> The conjugate acid is stabilized by resonance with one <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group and by hyper conjugation of <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> group.<br/><br/> <img src=\"assets\\st0155_f104c27175ea.png\" /> The conjugate acid is stabilized by resonance with only one <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group.<br/><br/>(III) Least basic, as the LP is used in aromaticity."
